{
  "raw": {
    "https://www.asbury.edu/about/offices/human-resources/jobs/postings/180933/": {
      "title": "Pastoral and Christian Ministries - Full Time, Tenure Track",
      "description": "Pastoral and Christian Ministries - Full Time, Tenure Track | www.asbury.edu Skip to content Undergraduate Start Here Programs Admissions Cost & Financial Aid Life at Asbury Student Support Athletics Find Your Major Virtual Tour Visit Apply Graduate Start Here Programs Graduate Student Admissions Cost & Aid Graduate Student Support Graduate Student Life Explore Degree Programs Schedule a Visit Start an Application Online Start Here Programs Online Admissions Cost & Aid Online Student Support Online Student Life Explore Online Programs Start an Application Who We Are Meet Our Students Meet the Classes Meet Our Faculty About Asbury Leadership Theological Heritage & Distinctives News and Media Events Accreditation Toggle search interface Toggle extended navigation Apply Visit Request info Give home About Pastoral and Christian Ministries – Full Time, Tenure Track Pastoral and Christian Ministries – Full Time, Tenure Track Job Details Department: Job Type: Faculty Status: Exempt Deadline: Until Filled APPLICATION PROCESS: Interested candidates should completed an employment application at application and include a letter of interest, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, and a statement describing the current vitality of your personal Christian faith. POSITION: The Christian Ministry Department, within the School of Christian Studies at Asbury University, invites applications and nominations for an open-rank, tenure-track position in Pastoral & Christian Ministries beginning August 2027. Ministry is an important dimension to the Asbury University campus and to the historic life of the church. The Ministry programs have a robust curriculum that informs each undergraduate students’ instruction in preparation for ministry, in use of bible and theology for ministry, and in cultivating a formative student learning experience. The position seeks a strong commitment to ministry, congregational and leadership experience, and excellent academic qualifications. INSTITUTIONAL COMMITMENT: Asbury University is an independent, Christian, liberal arts university in the Wesleyan-Holiness tradition. In the desire to be a more inclusive community, reflective of the Kingdom of God, we especially encourage applications from candidates with ethnic backgrounds that are underrepresented on our faculty and staff. At Asbury University, employees must display a committed and dynamic Christian faith along with the ability to support the University’s Wesleyan Holiness theological position, lifestyle standards, and mission. Candidates must agree, support and adhere to University policies and procedures, including the Faculty Manual, Community Standards Guidelines, Human Sexuality Statement, and the Standard of Conduct for employees. Asbury University does not discriminate based on race, national origin, gender, or handicap in its educational programs, activities, or employment practices. RESPONSIBILITIES: Teaching and program management activities equivalent to 24 credit-hours in an academic year. This would include teaching majors courses in undergraduate Pastoral, Educational, and Christian Ministries; teaching courses in the graduate Ministry Innovation program; co-maintaining the curriculum (recommending periodic modifications as desired); supervising program activities; advising students in the majors; serving on assigned department and university committees; and providing leadership and active participation in campus activities as a representative of the programs. ACADEMIC RANK: Academic rank at the Assistant or Associate Professor level commensurate with experience.  Salary and benefits are competitive with comparable institutions. REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS: Candidates should possess a strong academic foundation in Pastoral, Educational, or Christian Ministry, as well as congregational and leadership experience while on staff with a church or parachurch ministry. A doctorate in Ministry (Ph.D., D.Min.) or closely related field is expected. Doctoral candidates close to completion (all but dissertation) will be considered. DESIRED QUALIFICATIONS: Preference will be given to applicants with the most appropriate academic credentials, teaching experience in Ministry at the undergraduate or graduate level, and field experience in ministry and leadership. A marked enthusiasm for investing in student professional formation, along with an ability to articulate that vision, is desired. An inclination to organizational administration is desired. Online teaching or learning experience is not required but is an advantage for applicants; a willingness to adapt to distance-oriented teaching modalities is necessary, given the shifts taking place in higher education. A strong academic foundation in bible and theology is not required but is an advantage for applicants. COMPENSATION :  Compensation is competitive and dependent upon education and experience. Benefits include retirement (TIAA/CREF) and insurance plans. INQUIRY PROCESS: Questions may be directed to Prof. Caleigh Smith, Interim Chair of the Christian Ministry Department, caleigh.smith@asbury.edu , or Dr. Brian Shelton, Dean of the School of Christian Studies, brian.shelton@asbury.edu .  For more information on the School of Christians Studies see: School of Christian Studies One Macklem Drive • Wilmore, KY 40390 (859) 858-3511 Facebook Instagram Linkedin Youtube Mic Accreditation Calendar Campus Safety Chapel Directory Faculty Resources Jobs at Asbury Kinlaw Library My Asbury Site Accessibility Student Accounts This is Asbury Podcast Title IX © Copyright 2026 Asbury University Legal Notices Privacy Policy Title IX Non-Discrimination Student Code of Conduct Report an Issue with this Page Close navigation Apply Visit Request info Give Search Site Search Undergraduate Start Here Programs Admissions Cost & Financial Aid Life at Asbury Student Support Athletics Find Your Major Virtual Tour Visit Apply Graduate Start Here Programs Graduate Student Admissions Cost & Aid Graduate Student Support Graduate Student Life Explore Degree Programs Schedule a Visit Start an Application Online Start Here Programs Online Admissions Cost & Aid Online Student Support Online Student Life Explore Online Programs Start an Application Who We Are Meet Our Students Meet the Classes Meet Our Faculty About Asbury Leadership Theological Heritage & Distinctives News and Media Events Accreditation Athletics Alumni Alumni Home Reunion Alumni Board Ambassador Magazine Resources Chapel Campus Safety Faculty & Staff Directory Offices Registrar Provost Student Accounts Kinlaw Library Information for... Alumni Giving to Asbury More About Asbury About Asbury Life The College Tour Academy Dual Enrollment Title IX Conferences and Camps News & Media Calendar My Asbury Faculty & Staff Directory Secret Link We use cookies to ensure that we give you the best experience on our website. If you continue to use this site we will assume that you are happy with it. Accept"
    },
    "https://www.asbury.edu/about/offices/human-resources/jobs/postings/181646/": {
      "title": "Marketing - Full Time, Tenure Track",
      "description": "Marketing - Full Time, Tenure Track | www.asbury.edu Skip to content Undergraduate Start Here Programs Admissions Cost & Financial Aid Life at Asbury Student Support Athletics Find Your Major Virtual Tour Visit Apply Graduate Start Here Programs Graduate Student Admissions Cost & Aid Graduate Student Support Graduate Student Life Explore Degree Programs Schedule a Visit Start an Application Online Start Here Programs Online Admissions Cost & Aid Online Student Support Online Student Life Explore Online Programs Start an Application Who We Are Meet Our Students Meet the Classes Meet Our Faculty About Asbury Leadership Theological Heritage & Distinctives News and Media Events Accreditation Toggle search interface Toggle extended navigation Apply Visit Request info Give home About Marketing – Full Time, Tenure Track Marketing – Full Time, Tenure Track Job Details Department: Dayton School of Business Job Type: Faculty Status: Exempt Deadline: Until Filled APPLICATION PROCESS: Interested candidates should complete an employment application at application and include a letter of interest, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, and a statement describing the current vitality of your personal Christian faith. Applications available at jobs.asbury.edu POSITION: The Management and Marketing Department, within the Dayton School of Business at Asbury University, invites applications and nominations for an open-rank, tenure-track position in Marketing & Sales who will also serve as Director of the Asbury University Center for Professional Selling (AUCPS) beginning August 2027. We are seeking an excellent and engaging educator, committed to Asbury’s Christian mission and passionate about preparing students for a rapidly changing global marketplace. We particularly value candidates who: Bring an innovative and applied approach to Marketing and Sales, incorporating digital marketing, AI, analytics, emerging technologies, and contemporary industry practice. Create highly engaging learning experiences in person, online, and hybrid. Can teach across Marketing and Sales at undergraduate and graduate levels, including to a global and culturally diverse MBA audience. Bring meaningful professional and marketplace experience into the classroom. Are passionate about coaching and mentoring students and developing their professional capabilities. Can build strong relationships with corporate partners and industry leaders. As Director of AUCPS, the successful candidate will provide leadership for the Center, coach the nationally recognized Asbury Sales Team, develop corporate sponsorships and partnerships, mentor students, and support student recruitment. INSTITUTIONAL COMMITMENT: Asbury University is an independent, Christian, liberal arts university in the Wesleyan-Holiness tradition. In the desire to be a more inclusive community, reflective of the Kingdom of God, we especially encourage applications from women and from candidates from various ethnic backgrounds. At Asbury University, employees must display a committed and dynamic Christian faith along with the ability to support the University’s Wesleyan Holiness theological position, lifestyle standards, and mission. Candidates must agree, support and adhere to University policies and procedures – including the Faculty Manual, Community Standards Guidelines, Human Sexuality Statement, and the Standard of Conduct for employees. Asbury University does not discriminate on the basis of race, national origin, gender, or handicap in its educational programs, activities, or employment practices. DEPARTMENT: The Dayton School of Business serves more than 225 undergraduate and graduate students across Accounting, Business Administration, Finance, Marketing, and Sport Management, as well as MBA and Master of Science in Accounting programs. DSB is committed to creating a highly engaged business education where faith, academic excellence, and the marketplace come together, connecting students with entrepreneurs, executives, organizations, and opportunities locally and globally. RESPONSIBILITIES: Teach 24 credit hours in an academic year, as well as scholarship and research, academic advising, university service, accreditation support, and professional development. Teaching may include in-person, online, and hybrid courses. ACADEMIC RANK: Tenure track; Academic rank at the Assistant or Associate Professor level commensurate with experience. REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS: Terminal degree in Marketing, Sales, or a closely related field preferred. ABD candidates with a clear plan for degree completion will be considered. Candidates with an MBA or related master’s degree, five or more years of significant professional experience, and progress toward or a plan to complete a doctorate may be considered for a three-year rolling appointment. Significant professional experience in B2B sales, sales management, marketing, or related fields is highly valued. DESIRED QUALIFICATIONS: Preference will be given to applicants with the most appropriate academic credentials from an AACSB or ACBSP accredited institution, teaching experience, and professional and industry experience. COMPENSATION: Compensation is competitive and dependent upon education and experience. INQUIRY PROCESS: Questions may be directed to Prof. Michelle Smith, Chair of the Management and Marketing Department, mlsmith@asbury.edu , or Prof. Rob Lim, Dean of the Dayton School of Business, robin.lim@asbury.edu.  For more specific information regarding the Dayton School of Business see: Dayton School of Business One Macklem Drive • Wilmore, KY 40390 (859) 858-3511 Facebook Instagram Linkedin Youtube Mic Accreditation Calendar Campus Safety Chapel Directory Faculty Resources Jobs at Asbury Kinlaw Library My Asbury Site Accessibility Student Accounts This is Asbury Podcast Title IX © Copyright 2026 Asbury University Legal Notices Privacy Policy Title IX Non-Discrimination Student Code of Conduct 