    "https://www.asbury.edu/about/offices/human-resources/jobs/postings/172656/": {
      "title": "Social Work - Full-Time, Tenure Track",
      "description": "Social Work - Full-Time, Tenure Track | www.asbury.edu Skip to content Undergraduate Start Here Programs Admissions Cost & Financial Aid Life at Asbury Student Support Athletics Find Your Major Virtual Tour Visit Apply Graduate Start Here Programs Graduate Student Admissions Cost & Aid Graduate Student Support Graduate Student Life Explore Degree Programs Schedule a Visit Start an Application Online Start Here Programs Online Admissions Cost & Aid Online Student Support Online Student Life Explore Online Programs Start an Application Who We Are Meet Our Students Meet the Classes Meet Our Faculty About Asbury Leadership Theological Heritage & Distinctives News and Media Events Accreditation Toggle search interface Toggle extended navigation Apply Visit Request info Give home About Social Work – Full-Time, Tenure Track Social Work – Full-Time, Tenure Track Job Details Department: Social Work Job Type: Faculty Status: Exempt Deadline: Until Filled APPLICATION PROCESS: Interested candidates should complete an employment application and include a letter of interest, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, and a statement describing the current vitality of your personal Christian faith.  Applications available at jobs.asbury.edu POSITION: The CSWE-accredited Bachelor of Arts in Social Work (BASW) Program, within the College of Arts, Humanities & Social Sciences at Asbury University, invites applications and nominations for an Assistant Professor, Tenure-Track position in Social Work beginning August 2027. RESPONSIBILITIES: Teach 24 credit hours in an academic year (introductory and upper-level courses; in-seat and online) Advise social work majors Serve on assigned university committees Course and curriculum design and development ACADEMIC RANK: Tenure track, Assistant Professor. Salary and benefits are competitive with comparable institutions. REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS: A Ph.D. in Social Work is preferred ABD candidates will be considered MSW from a CSWE-accredited program with five years of post-MSW experience Deep commitment to the integration of the Christian faith, the liberal arts, and social work education Evidence of personal commitment to Jesus Christ, active involvement in the local church, and community engagement that integrates biblical and NASW Cod of Ethics and values Evidence of pedagogical skills and scholarship with prior social work education teaching experience Ability to teach beginning and advanced courses Experience developing curriculum aligned with CSWE/EPAS competencies (in-seat and online) Strong interpersonal skills PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Experience with CSWE accreditation, specifically program assessment, curriculum development, and course design Higher education teaching experience in social work practice Micro/clinical experience with diverse populations Experience with learning management systems (LMS) INSTITUTIONAL COMMITMENT: Asbury University is an independent, Christian, liberal arts university in the Wesleyan-Holiness tradition. In our desire to be a more inclusive community, reflective of the Kingdom of God, we especially encourage applications from women and candidates from diverse ethnic backgrounds. At Asbury University, employees must display a committed and dynamic Christian faith along with the ability to support the University’s Wesleyan Holiness theological position, lifestyle standards, and mission. Candidates must agree, support, and adhere to University policies and procedures – including the Faculty Manual, Community Standards Guidelines, Human Sexuality Statement, and the Standard of Conduct for employees. Asbury University does not discriminate on the basis of race, national origin, gender, or disability in its educational programs, activities, or employment practices. For more information about the Social Work Department see: Social Work Department One Macklem Drive • Wilmore, KY 40390 (859) 858-3511 Facebook Instagram Linkedin Youtube Mic Accreditation Calendar Campus Safety Chapel Directory Faculty Resources Jobs at Asbury Kinlaw Library My Asbury Site Accessibility Student Accounts This is Asbury Podcast Title IX © Copyright 2026 Asbury University Legal Notices Privacy Policy Title IX Non-Discrimination Student Code of Conduct Report an Issue with this Page Close navigation Apply Visit Request info Give Search Site Search Undergraduate Start Here Programs Admissions Cost & Financial Aid Life at Asbury Student Support Athletics Find Your Major Virtual Tour Visit Apply Graduate Start Here Programs Graduate Student Admissions Cost & Aid Graduate Student Support Graduate Student Life Explore Degree Programs Schedule a Visit Start an Application Online Start Here Programs Online Admissions Cost & Aid Online Student Support Online Student Life Explore Online Programs Start an Application Who We Are Meet Our Students Meet the Classes Meet Our Faculty About Asbury Leadership Theological Heritage & Distinctives News and Media Events Accreditation Athletics Alumni Alumni Home Reunion Alumni Board Ambassador Magazine Resources Chapel Campus Safety Faculty & Staff Directory Offices Registrar Provost Student Accounts Kinlaw Library Information for... Alumni Giving to Asbury More About Asbury About Asbury Life The College Tour Academy Dual Enrollment Title IX Conferences and Camps News & Media Calendar My Asbury Faculty & Staff Directory Secret Link We use cookies to ensure that we give you the best experience on our website. If you continue to use this site we will assume that you are happy with it. Accept"
