    "https://www.asbury.edu/about/offices/human-resources/jobs/postings/175924/": {
      "title": "Academic Records System Coordinator",
      "description": "Academic Records System Coordinator | www.asbury.edu Skip to content Undergraduate Start Here Programs Admissions Cost & Financial Aid Life at Asbury Student Support Athletics Find Your Major Virtual Tour Visit Apply Graduate Start Here Programs Graduate Student Admissions Cost & Aid Graduate Student Support Graduate Student Life Explore Degree Programs Schedule a Visit Start an Application Online Start Here Programs Online Admissions Cost & Aid Online Student Support Online Student Life Explore Online Programs Start an Application Who We Are Meet Our Students Meet the Classes Meet Our Faculty About Asbury Leadership Theological Heritage & Distinctives News and Media Events Accreditation Toggle search interface Toggle extended navigation Apply Visit Request info Give home About Academic Records System Coordinator Academic Records System Coordinator Job Details Department: Administrative Support Job Type: Staff Status: Exempt Deadline: Until Filled Asbury University is looking for a qualified candidate to fill the open Academic Records System Coordinator position. Apply at jobs.asbury.edu Job Title: Academic Records System Coordinator Reports to: University Registrar FLSA Classification: Exempt Job Purpose: The Academic Records System Coordinator leverages analytical and technical expertise to manage University academic records systems from initial enrollment through graduation. This position exercises independent judgement in maintaining and evaluating student academic data across multiple technology platforms including the Student Information System (Anthology Student), the Degree Progress Audit (Student Portal), Slate CRM, the CollegeSource Transfer Equivalency System, and Curriculog. The Academic Records System Coordinator interprets complex academic data, configures system logic, and collaborates with Information Technology to implement technology‑enabled solutions that support seamless academic data workflows across departments. This position plays a critical role in maintaining the reliability of institutional data structures, troubleshooting advanced system challenges, and driving innovation in academic records management. An important part of the position is supporting the ministry and mission of the University and advancing the academic excellence and spiritual vitality of our University and students. Each employee plays an important role in the development of the Christian faith in our students. Essential Functions: Serves as the primary authority for all undergraduate Degree Progress Audit record reviews and updates, including individual student audits at matriculation and after program changes, as well as batch updates for standardized academic requirements. Interprets approved curricular changes and independently configures new academic programs, areas of study, courses, and course lists within the Student Information System (SIS) using advanced system logic. Functions as the Registrar’s Office technical liaison to Information Technology, conducting advanced system testing, documenting and diagnosing issues, and implementing solutions that enhance performance across technology platforms. Oversees degree application process for undergraduate students, analyzes student records for graduation eligibility, and posts degree conferrals to the academic record. Executes complex SIS updates affecting enrollment and academic status, including program changes, substitution/waiver entries, application of institutional credit, and other data elements requiring high‑level accuracy and discretion. Works closely with Associate Registrar to manage the SIS academic record module background configuration, ensuring data consistency across interconnected system components such as term and catalog year setup, registration controls, system workflows, and electronic student documentation. Provides expert guidance to faculty advisors and current students regarding degree requirements, curriculum structure, and the Degree Progress Audit. Applies advanced analytical thinking to evaluate system workflows, identify inefficiencies, and recommend technology‑based improvements that enhance operational effectiveness. Prepares and delivers training for Registrar’s Office staff and campus partners regarding important system functionality and processes. Develops and maintains comprehensive technical documentation for SIS and Degree Progress Audit processes, system maintenance, and recurring operational tasks. Collaborates with undergraduate Admissions to receive, evaluate, and process incoming and returning student data. Plans, organizes, and prepares individualized student materials for office participation in freshman orientation events (Eagle Days). Assists the Registrar and Associate Registrar in monitoring student performance and sends communications related to any violations of policies or regulations, including probations and suspensions. Supports undergraduate students with enrollment, registration, and course scheduling details. Identifies applicable institutional resources to help students reach their academic goals. Provides outstanding service to students and other internal and external constituents. Regular and punctual attendance at work. Must be available for evening and weekend registration, as requested, and for Baccalaureate and Commencement activities. Other support duties or special projects, as needed. Physical Requirements: While performing the duties of this job, the employee is regularly required to talk or hear. The employee frequently is required to stand; walk; use hands to finger, handle or feel; and reach with hands and arms. This position requires the ability to occasionally lift office products and supplies, up to 20 pounds. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work : This is a full-time position, and hours of work and days are Monday through Friday, 8:00 a.m. to 5 p.m. Travel: No travel is expected for this position. Qualifications : Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college is required. Strong computer skills, including MS Word, Excel, and Outlook. Ability and interest in learning new technology systems is a must. Proactive and solutions-oriented approach to work. Excellent interpersonal, written, and oral communication skills. Strong analytical and organizational skills; attention to detail. Proven customer service skills, with the ability to kindly explain and uphold policy. Ability to uphold FERPA and keep information confidential required. Independent judgment and administrative assistance experience necessary. A committed and dynamic Christian faith is vital along with the ability to support the University’s theological position, lifestyle standards and mission. Other Duties : Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. Institutional Commitment: Asbury University is an independent, Christian, liberal arts university in the Wesleyan-Holiness tradition. In the desire to be a more inclusive community, reflective of the Kingdom of God, we especially encourage applications from women and from candidates from various ethnic backgrounds. At Asbury University, employees must display a committed and dynamic Christian faith along with the ability to support the University’s theological position, lifestyle standards, and mission. Candidates must agree, support and adhere to University policies and procedures – including the Faculty Manual, Community Standards Guidelines, Human Sexuality Statement, and the Standard of Conduct for employees. Asbury University does not discriminate on the basis of race, national origin, gender, or handicap in its educational programs, activities, or employment practices. One Macklem Drive • Wilmore, KY 40390 (859) 858-3511 Facebook Instagram Linkedin Youtube Mic Accreditation Calendar Campus Safety Chapel Directory Faculty Resources Jobs at Asbury Kinlaw Library My Asbury Site Accessibility Student Accounts This is Asbury Podcast Title IX © Copyright 2026 Asbury University Legal Notices Privacy Policy Title IX Non-Discrimination Student Code of Conduct Report an Issue with this Page Close navigation Apply Visit Request info Give Search Site Search Undergraduate Start Here Programs Admissions Cost & Financial Aid Life at Asbury Student Support Athletics Find Your Major Virtual Tour Visit Apply Graduate Start Here Programs Graduate Student Admissions Cost & Aid Graduate Student Support Graduate Student Life Explore Degree Programs Schedule a Visit Start an Application Online Start Here Programs Online Admissions Cost & Aid Online Student Support Online Student Life Explore Online Programs Start an Application Who We Are Meet Our Students Meet the Classes Meet Our Faculty About Asbury Leadership Theological Heritage & Distinctives News and Media Events Accreditation Athletics Alumni Alumni Home Reunion Alumni Board Ambassador Magazine Resources Chapel Campus Safety Faculty & Staff Directory Offices Registrar Provost Student Accounts Kinlaw Library Information for... Alumni Giving to Asbury More About Asbury About Asbury Life The College Tour Academy Dual Enrollment Title IX Conferences and Camps News & Media Calendar My Asbury Faculty & Staff Directory Secret Link We use cookies to ensure that we give you the best experience on our website. If you continue to use this site we will assume that you are happy with it. Accept"
    },
    "https://www.asbury.edu/about/offices/human-resources/jobs/postings/178007/": {
      "title": "Development Services Assistant",
      "description": "Development Services Assistant | www.asbury.edu Skip to content Undergraduate Start Here Programs Admissions Cost & Financial Aid Life at Asbury Student Support Athletics Find Your Major Virtual Tour Visit Apply Graduate Start Here Programs Graduate Student Admissions Cost & Aid Graduate Student Support Graduate Student Life Explore Degree Programs Schedule a Visit Start an Application Online Start Here Programs Online Admissions Cost & Aid Online Student Support Online Student Life Explore Online Programs Start an Application Who We Are Meet Our Students Meet the Classes Meet Our Faculty About Asbury Leadership Theological Heritage & Distinctives News and Media Events Accreditation Toggle search interface Toggle extended navigation Apply Visit Request info Give home About Development Services Assistant Development Services Assistant Job Details Department: Administrative Support Job Type: Staff Status: Non-Exempt Deadline: Until Filled Asbury University is looking for a qualified candidate to fill the open Part Time Development Services Assistant position. Apply at jobs.asbury.edu Job Title :        Development Services Assistant Reports to : Director of Development Services Status: Non-exempt Job Purpose : The Development Services Assistant works with the Assistant Director of Development Services to manage the information services support areas of the Development Office. This part-time position will assist with gift processing and reporting and with responding to information requests for fundraising data. The Assistant will also work to develop and execute a comprehensive stewardship plan to enhance the relationship between Asbury University and its donors. The Assistant will work with confidential information on a daily basis.  An important part of the position is supporting the mission of the University and advancing the academic excellence and spiritual vitality of our University and students. Essential Functions: Responsible for the proper acceptance, tracking, recording and reporting of charitable gifts in accordance with University policy, state and federal laws, and IRS regulations. Manage the tracking of annual giving and campaign pledges, including pledge and payment entry in Slate, management of digital/paper documentation, attributing to campaigns and appeals, and tracking of naming opportunities. Manage recurring/monthly giving and payroll deduction programs. Coordinate communication on declined and/or expiring enrollments. Generate reports regarding charitable gifts, commitments, prospects and donors. Manage communication to University departments/programs informing them of charitable gifts received for their area. Maintain an accurate and complete filing system for charitable giving. Develop strategies to improve the integrity of donor database records. Assist with various development fundraising efforts as needed, including special events. Performs other duties as assigned. Physical requirements: While performing the duties of this job, the employee is regularly required to talk or hear. The employee frequently is required to stand; walk; use hands to finger, handle or feel; and reach with hands and arms. This position requires the ability to occasionally lift items, up to 25 pounds. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work : This is a part-time position, and normal work hours are within Monday through Friday, 8:00 a.m. to 5 p.m. Travel: No travel is expected for this position. Qualifications : The Development Services Assistant should be highly detail oriented with proven accuracy with data entry and analysis. The successful candidate must possess problem solving and research skills, have an understanding of fundraising support services, and be able to handle confidential information. Experience with Slate or similar fundraising software is preferred. Experience using Microsoft Office software is required. High School diploma or equivalent is required, with some college preferred, along with a minimum of two to three years of experience in a related field. A committed and dynamic Christian faith is vital with the ability to support the University’s theological position, lifestyle standards and mission. Other Duties : Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities may change at any time with or without notice. Institutional Commitment: Asbury University is an independent, Christian, liberal arts university in the Wesleyan-Holiness tradition. In the desire to be a more inclusive community, reflective of the Kingdom of God, we especially encourage applications from women and from candidates from various ethnic backgrounds. At Asbury University, employees must display a committed and dynamic Christian faith along with the ability to support the University’s theological position, lifestyle standards, and mission. Candidates must agree, support and adhere to University policies and procedures – including the Faculty Manual, Community Standards Guidelines, Human Sexuality Statement, and the Standard of Conduct for employees. Asbury University does not discriminate on the basis of race, national origin, gender, or handicap in its educational programs, activities, or employment practices. One Macklem Drive • Wilmore, KY 40390 (859) 858-3511 Facebook Instagram Linkedin Youtube Mic Accreditation Calendar Campus Safety Chapel Directory Faculty Resources Jobs at Asbury Kinlaw Library My Asbury Site Accessibility Student Accounts This is Asbury Podcast Title IX © Copyright 2026 Asbury University Legal Notices Privacy Policy Title IX Non-Discrimination Student Code of Conduct Report an Issue with this Page Close navigation Apply Visit Request info Give Search Site Search Undergraduate Start Here Programs Admissions Cost & Financial Aid Life at Asbury Student Support Athletics Find Your Major Virtual Tour Visit Apply Graduate Start Here Programs Graduate Student Admissions Cost & Aid Graduate Student Support Graduate Student Life Explore Degree Programs Schedule a Visit Start an Application Online Start Here Programs Online Admissions Cost & Aid Online Student Support Online Student Life Explore Online Programs Start an Application Who We Are Meet Our Students Meet the Classes Meet Our Faculty About Asbury Leadership Theological Heritage & Distinctives News and Media Events Accreditation Athletics Alumni Alumni Home Reunion Alumni Board Ambassador Magazine Resources Chapel Campus Safety Faculty & Staff Directory Offices Registrar Provost Student Accounts Kinlaw Library Information for... Alumni Giving to Asbury More About Asbury About Asbury Life The College Tour Academy Dual Enrollment Title IX Conferences and Camps News & Media Calendar My Asbury Faculty & Staff Directory Secret Link We use cookies to ensure that we give you the best experience on our website. If you continue to use this site we will assume that you are happy with it. Accept"
    },
    "https://www.asbury.edu/about/offices/human-resources/jobs/postings/180259/": {
      "title": "Staff Assistant - Center for Academic Excellence",
      "description": "Staff Assistant - Center for Academic Excellence | www.asbury.edu Skip to content Undergraduate Start Here Programs Admissions Cost & Financial Aid Life at Asbury Student Support Athletics Find Your Major Virtual Tour Visit Apply Graduate Start Here Programs Graduate Student Admissions Cost & Aid Graduate Student Support Graduate Student Life Explore Degree Programs Schedule a Visit Start an Application Online Start Here Programs Online Admissions Cost & Aid Online Student Support Online Student Life Explore Online Programs Start an Application Who We Are Meet Our Students Meet the Classes Meet Our Faculty About Asbury Leadership Theological Heritage & Distinctives News and Media Events Accreditation Toggle search interface Toggle extended navigation Apply Visit Request info Give home About Staff Assistant – Center for Academic Excellence Staff Assistant – Center for Academic Excellence Job Details Department: Administrative Support Job Type: Staff Status: Non-Exempt Deadline: Until Filled Job Purpose: The Staff Assistant serves as reception to Center for Academic Excellence (CAE) and coordinates their daily operations. An important part of the position is supporting the ministry and mission of the University and advancing the academic excellence and spiritual vitality of our University and students. Each employee plays an important role in the development of the Christian faith in our students. Responsibilities: Manage activities of the Center for Academic Excellence including, but not limited to assistance for students requesting tutoring information supervision of peer educators (writing consultants and course tutors) supervision of other CAE student employees Coordinate course tutoring, writing consulting, and academic coaching scheduling and appointments Assist CAE Director in peer educator development and training Provide support for Academic Accessibility Resources (AAR) Oversee scheduling and administration of AAR testing accommodations for exams taken in the CAE Assist CAE Director in development and implementation of policies and procedures related to academic support and student success Assist CAE Director in creation of materials, resources, and activities related to student academic success Maintain records of CAE services usage and produce visualizations of the data Maintain cleanliness and professionalism of the CAE space Other duties as assigned Physical Requirements While performing the duties of this job, the employee is regularly required to talk or hear. The employee frequently is required to stand; walk; use hands to finger, handle or feel; and reach with hands and arms. This position requires the ability to occasionally lift office products and supplies, up to 20 pounds. Position Requirements This is a full-time, on-site, 10-month position, and hours of work and days are Monday through Friday, 8:00 a.m. to 5 p.m. Potential exists to work some evenings and weekends. Travel Requirements: No travel is expected for this position. Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree, preferably in Education, English, or some related field Experience with tutoring, either as a tutor or as a tutoring supervisor Supports the vision and goals of Asbury University and the Center for Academic Excellence Excellent organizational skills; attention to detail Strong ability to multi-task and handle frequent interruptions Works well in a busy office environment Shows initiative for problem solving and project management Competent in the use of technology Inviting, helpful disposition Enjoys interacting with students and faculty Knowledgeable of available resources and personnel on AU campus and surrounding area A committed and dynamic Christian faith is vital along with the ability to support the University’s theological position, lifestyle standards and mission. Other Duties: Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities may change at any time with or without notice. Apply at https://jobs.asbury.edu/ One Macklem Drive • Wilmore, KY 40390 (859) 858-3511 Facebook Instagram Linkedin Youtube Mic Accreditation Calendar Campus Safety Chapel Directory Faculty Resources Jobs at Asbury Kinlaw Library My Asbury Site Accessibility Student Accounts This is Asbury Podcast Title IX © Copyright 2026 Asbury University Legal Notices Privacy Policy Title IX Non-Discrimination Student Code of Conduct Report an Issue with this Page Close navigation Apply Visit Request info Give Search Site Search Undergraduate Start Here Programs Admissions Cost & Financial Aid Life at Asbury Student Support Athletics Find Your Major Virtual Tour Visit Apply Graduate Start Here Programs Graduate Student Admissions Cost & Aid Graduate Student Support Graduate Student Life Explore Degree Programs Schedule a Visit Start an Application Online Start Here Programs Online Admissions Cost & Aid Online Student Support Online Student Life Explore Online Programs Start an Application Who We Are Meet Our Students Meet the Classes Meet Our Faculty About Asbury Leadership Theological Heritage & Distinctives News and Media Events Accreditation Athletics Alumni Alumni Home Reunion Alumni Board Ambassador Magazine Resources Chapel Campus Safety Faculty & Staff Directory Offices Registrar Provost Student Accounts Kinlaw Library Information for... Alumni Giving to Asbury More About Asbury About Asbury Life The College Tour Academy Dual Enrollment Title IX Conferences and Camps News & Media Calendar My Asbury Faculty & Staff Directory Secret Link We use cookies to ensure that we give you the best experience on our website. If you continue to use this site we will assume that you are happy with it. Accept"
    },
    "https://www.asbury.edu/about/offices/human-resources/jobs/postings/182383/": {
      "title": "Staff Assistant - Center for Wholeness and Wellness",
      "description": "Staff Assistant - Center for Wholeness and Wellness | www.asbury.edu Skip to content Undergraduate Start Here Programs Admissions Cost & Financial Aid Life at Asbury Student Support Athletics Find Your Major Virtual Tour Visit Apply Graduate Start Here Programs Graduate Student Admissions Cost & Aid Graduate Student Support Graduate Student Life Explore Degree Programs Schedule a Visit Start an Application Online Start Here Programs Online Admissions Cost & Aid Online Student Support Online Student Life Explore Online Programs Start an Application Who We Are Meet Our Students Meet the Classes Meet Our Faculty About Asbury Leadership Theological Heritage & Distinctives News and Media Events Accreditation Toggle search interface Toggle extended navigation Apply Visit Request info Give home About Staff Assistant – Center for Wholeness and Wellness Staff Assistant – Center for Wholeness and Wellness Job Details Department: Administrative Support Job Type: Staff Status: Non-Exempt Deadline: Until Filled Reports to: Associate Dean of Wholeness and Wellness and Director of Student Health Services FLSA Classification: Non-exempt, Full-time, 40 hours/week, 52 weeks per year Position Summary: The Center for Wholeness and Wellness Staff Assistant supports both Student Health Services and the Center for Counseling and maintains the clerical responsibilities for the operations of both, as a dynamic member of the team Nature of Duties & Responsibilities: In addition to reception duties in Student Health Services and The Center for Counseling: Provides clerical and telephone support for the administrator and other office staff Processing, maintaining and releasing medical records Billing and general ledger Scheduling student appointments Assisting with student health insurance claims Managing statistical databases for departmental and State reports Handling routine interdepartmental and off-campus business matters Updating departmental web pages Create and maintain semester schedule for all counselors Screens Health Services Required Admission Documents for completion and compliance Supervising and managing the schedule and workload of the student worker Perform clerical functions such as distribution of mail, photocopying, updating & maintaining forms, filing and ordering supplies Other duties as assigned Experience and Training: 1-2 years clerical and reception experience (medical office experience preferred); strong working knowledge of Microsoft Office programs as well as high computer literacy; excellent written and oral communication skills; ability to multitask and prioritize; understanding the confidentiality of HIPPA laws & requirements, strong interpersonal skills a must. Supervision Received: Specific instructions from supervisors and standardized procedures. Supervision of Others: Oversees student worker Education: High school education or equivalent with courses in business practices preferred. Other Requirements: A committed and dynamic Christian faith is vital along with the ability to support the University’s theological position, lifestyle standards and mission. One Macklem Drive • Wilmore, KY 40390 (859) 858-3511 Facebook Instagram Linkedin Youtube Mic Accreditation Calendar Campus Safety Chapel Directory Faculty Resources Jobs at Asbury Kinlaw Library My Asbury Site Accessibility Student Accounts This is Asbury Podcast Title IX © Copyright 2026 Asbury University Legal Notices Privacy Policy Title IX Non-Discrimination Student Code of Conduct Report an Issue with this Page Close navigation Apply Visit Request info Give Search Site Search Undergraduate Start Here Programs Admissions Cost & Financial Aid Life at Asbury Student Support Athletics Find Your Major Virtual Tour Visit Apply Graduate Start Here Programs Graduate Student Admissions Cost & Aid Graduate Student Support Graduate Student Life Explore Degree Programs Schedule a Visit Start an Application Online Start Here Programs Online Admissions Cost & Aid Online Student Support Online Student Life Explore Online Programs Start an Application Who We Are Meet Our Students Meet the Classes Meet Our Faculty About Asbury Leadership Theological Heritage & Distinctives News and Media Events Accreditation Athletics Alumni Alumni Home Reunion Alumni Board Ambassador Magazine Resources Chapel Campus Safety Faculty & Staff Directory Offices Registrar Provost Student Accounts Kinlaw Library Information for... Alumni Giving to Asbury More About Asbury About Asbury Life The College Tour Academy Dual Enrollment Title IX Conferences and Camps News & Media Calendar My Asbury Faculty & Staff Directory Secret Link We use cookies to ensure that we give you the best experience on our website. If you continue to use this site we will assume that you are happy with it. Accept"
