    "https://www.asbury.edu/about/offices/human-resources/jobs/postings/171032/": {
      "title": "Staff Assistant - Department of Nursing",
      "description": "Staff Assistant - Department of Nursing | www.asbury.edu Skip to content Undergraduate Start Here Programs Admissions Cost & Financial Aid Life at Asbury Student Support Athletics Find Your Major Virtual Tour Visit Apply Graduate Start Here Programs Graduate Student Admissions Cost & Aid Graduate Student Support Graduate Student Life Explore Degree Programs Schedule a Visit Start an Application Online Start Here Programs Online Admissions Cost & Aid Online Student Support Online Student Life Explore Online Programs Start an Application Who We Are Meet Our Students Meet the Classes Meet Our Faculty About Asbury Leadership Theological Heritage & Distinctives News and Media Events Accreditation Toggle search interface Toggle extended navigation Apply Visit Request info Give home About Staff Assistant – Department of Nursing Staff Assistant – Department of Nursing Job Details Department: Administrative Support Job Type: Staff Status: Exempt Deadline: Until Filled Applications available at jobs.asbury.edu POSITION: Full-time Staff Assistant position beginning January 2027 SHAW SCHOOL OF SCIENCES INFORMATION: Asbury University announces a full-time staff position in the Department of Nursing to begin in January 2027 providing administrative support to the faculty and staff of the Department of Nursing. RESPONSIBILITIES: Provide administrative support to the Nursing program faculty and staff. Answer telephone calls for the Department of Nursing. Receive and assist nursing students, visitors, and other guests to the Department of Nursing. Provide information and answer general questions concerning the Department of Nursing. Create, organize, and maintain office and nursing student records from application to completion/withdrawal from the program in compliance with accreditation and regulatory body standards. Provide administrative support and compile data for nursing administrator as needed for accreditation and regulatory body reporting. Assist in preparation and organization of advisory board committee meetings. Assist in facilitating the completion and maintenance of clinical affiliation agreements and CastleBranch requirements. Assist with orientation of part-time and full-time faculty. Monitor and maintain office supply inventory. Assist in making purchases and budget tracking. Assist in preparing agendas and meeting minutes. Other duties as assigned. QUALIFICATIONS: A minimum of an Associate Degree in business administration or secretarial science or similar field. Two years of experience working in the field providing secretarial or clerical support. INSTITUTIONAL COMMITMENT: Asbury University is an independent, Christian liberal arts university in the Wesleyan-Holiness tradition. In the desire to be a more inclusive community, reflective of the Kingdom of God, we especially encourage candidate applications from various ethnic backgrounds. At Asbury University, employees must display a committed and dynamic Christian faith along with the ability to support the University’s Wesleyan Holiness theological position, lifestyle standards, and mission. Candidates must agree, support and adhere to university policies and procedures – including the Faculty Manual, Community Standards Guidelines, Human Sexuality Statement, and the Standard of Conduct for employees. Asbury University does not discriminate on the basis of race, national origin, gender, or handicap in its educational programs, activities, or employment practices COMPENSATION: Compensation is competitive and dependent upon education and experience. Benefits include retirement (TIAA/CREF) and insurance plans. INQUIRY PROCESS: Questions may be directed to Dr. Connie Lamb, Department of Nursing, Chair. Connie.Lamb@Asbury.edu Interested candidates should email a letter of interest, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, and a statement describing the current vitality of your personal Christian faith to human.resources@asbury.edu or mail to: Human Resources Asbury University 1 Macklem Drive Wilmore, KY 40390 One Macklem Drive • Wilmore, KY 40390 (859) 858-3511 Facebook Instagram Linkedin Youtube Mic Accreditation Calendar Campus Safety Chapel Directory Faculty Resources Jobs at Asbury Kinlaw Library My Asbury Site Accessibility Student Accounts This is Asbury Podcast Title IX © Copyright 2026 Asbury University Legal Notices Privacy Policy Title IX Non-Discrimination Student Code of Conduct Report an Issue with this Page Close navigation Apply Visit Request info Give Search Site Search Undergraduate Start Here Programs Admissions Cost & Financial Aid Life at Asbury Student Support Athletics Find Your Major Virtual Tour Visit Apply Graduate Start Here Programs Graduate Student Admissions Cost & Aid Graduate Student Support Graduate Student Life Explore Degree Programs Schedule a Visit Start an Application Online Start Here Programs Online Admissions Cost & Aid Online Student Support Online Student Life Explore Online Programs Start an Application Who We Are Meet Our Students Meet the Classes Meet Our Faculty About Asbury Leadership Theological Heritage & Distinctives News and Media Events Accreditation Athletics Alumni Alumni Home Reunion Alumni Board Ambassador Magazine Resources Chapel Campus Safety Faculty & Staff Directory Offices Registrar Provost Student Accounts Kinlaw Library Information for... Alumni Giving to Asbury More About Asbury About Asbury Life The College Tour Academy Dual Enrollment Title IX Conferences and Camps News & Media Calendar My Asbury Faculty & Staff Directory Secret Link We use cookies to ensure that we give you the best experience on our website. If you continue to use this site we will assume that you are happy with it. Accept"
    },
    "https://www.asbury.edu/about/offices/human-resources/jobs/postings/180333/": {
      "title": "Staff Assistant - Student Life",
      "description": "Staff Assistant - Student Life | www.asbury.edu Skip to content Undergraduate Start Here Programs Admissions Cost & Financial Aid Life at Asbury Student Support Athletics Find Your Major Virtual Tour Visit Apply Graduate Start Here Programs Graduate Student Admissions Cost & Aid Graduate Student Support Graduate Student Life Explore Degree Programs Schedule a Visit Start an Application Online Start Here Programs Online Admissions Cost & Aid Online Student Support Online Student Life Explore Online Programs Start an Application Who We Are Meet Our Students Meet the Classes Meet Our Faculty About Asbury Leadership Theological Heritage & Distinctives News and Media Events Accreditation Toggle search interface Toggle extended navigation Apply Visit Request info Give home About Staff Assistant – Student Life Staff Assistant – Student Life Job Details Department: Administrative Support Job Type: Staff Status: Non-Exempt Deadline: Until Filled Job Purpose: Provide support for the Student Life departments located in the Student Center, including Spiritual Life/Chapel Attendance, Community Life, Conference Services, and the Office of the Vice President. An important part of the position is supporting the ministry and mission of the University and advancing the academic excellence and spiritual vitality of our University and students. Each employee plays an important role in the development of the Christian faith in our students. Essential Functions: Serve as the initial point of contact via phone, email, and in person for students, parents and departments who have general Student Life questions, referring inquiries to others as needed. Assign seats for Chapel each semester by class identity, including special arrangements for students with seating accommodations approved by Academic Accessibility Resources. Reserve Chapel seats for visiting groups (Board of Trustees, Alumni Board, Admissions guests, etc.) and notify students whose seats are needed. Update and print attendance rosters biweekly for the Chapel Attendance binders. Be familiar with the iAttended chapel attendance software to answer student questions and troubleshoot when possible. Manage the application process for students seeking approval to live off campus or be granted a meal plan reduction or exemption. Assist with housing occupancy management and data entry/reconciliation of housing assignments/leases. Oversee the checkout of keys for the Student Life golf carts and Prayer House, checkout of tablecloths, and daily usage of the third-floor conference room. Manage communication and table reservations by external groups participating in the Activities Fair. Provide support for other events, such as Eagle Days, Welcome Weekend, Family Weekend, and Commencement, as needed. Manage students’ class identity data and generate class email distribution lists and directories for use by class advisors. Manage registration holds in Anthology for students who have not completed Title IX training. Submit and follow up on changes to Student Life website. Update and distribute the Student Life directory and org chart. Participate in Student Life divisional meetings and trainings. Make arrangements for Student Life team meetings (order food, set up, clean up, etc.). Make space reservations in Mazevo and submit ITS sound requests for events as needed. Submit Facilities work orders for custodial, maintenance, and room setup/teardown needs. Create signage and basic fliers in Canva. Prepare check requests, payment approvals and other financial documents as needed. Cross-train and serve as a backup for Eagle Outlet/CPO, HICCUP Coffee Shop, and Windsor Manor operations as needed. Take the HICCUP daily deposit to the Cashier’s Office. Assist with seasonal decoration of the Student Center and other campus spaces. Perform general office duties: answer the phone, pick up and distribute mail, welcome guests, create a space of hospitality for visitors, data entry, order and organize office supplies, submit monthly copier usage report, keep common areas in Student Life space tidy and organized. Other duties as assigned. Physical Requirements: While performing the duties of this job, the employee is regularly required to talk or hear. The employee frequently is required to stand; walk; use hands to finger, handle or feel; and reach with hands and arms. This position requires the ability to occasionally lift office products and supplies, up to 20 pounds. Reports to: Administrative Assistant to the Vice President of Student Life Position Type/Expected Hours of Work: This is a full-time, 12-month, on-site position. Days and hours of work are Monday through Friday, 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. Although rare, potential exists to work some evenings and weekends. Travel: No travel is expected for this position. Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree preferred. High school education or equivalent with courses in business practices; preferable training as an administrative professional or the equivalent college experience. Prefer 2 to 3 years office experience. Proficient computer skills, including Microsoft Word, Excel, and Outlook. Experience with Canva is preferred. Strong organizational skills. Attention to detail. Effective communication skills. Outstanding customer service. Ability to work in a multi-tasking environment with minimal supervision. A committed and dynamic Christian faith is vital along with the ability to support the University’s theological position, lifestyle standards and mission. Other Duties : Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities may change at any time with or without notice. Institutional Commitment: Asbury University is an independent, Christian, liberal arts university in the Wesleyan-Holiness tradition. In the desire to be a more inclusive community, reflective of the Kingdom of God, we especially encourage applications from women and from candidates from various ethnic backgrounds. At Asbury University, employees must display a committed and dynamic Christian faith along with the ability to support the University’s theological position, lifestyle standards, and mission. Candidates must agree, support and adhere to University policies and procedures – including the Faculty Manual, Community Standards Guidelines, Human Sexuality Statement, and the Standard of Conduct for employees. Asbury University does not discriminate on the basis of race, national origin, gender, or handicap in its educational programs, activities, or employment practices. One Macklem Drive • Wilmore, KY 40390 (859) 858-3511 Facebook Instagram Linkedin Youtube Mic Accreditation Calendar Campus Safety Chapel Directory Faculty Resources Jobs at Asbury Kinlaw Library My Asbury Site Accessibility Student Accounts This is Asbury Podcast Title IX © Copyright 2026 Asbury University Legal Notices Privacy Policy Title IX Non-Discrimination Student Code of Conduct Report an Issue with this Page Close navigation Apply Visit Request info Give Search Site Search Undergraduate Start Here Programs Admissions Cost & Financial Aid Life at Asbury Student Support Athletics Find Your Major Virtual Tour Visit Apply Graduate Start Here Programs Graduate Student Admissions Cost & Aid Graduate Student Support Graduate Student Life Explore Degree Programs Schedule a Visit Start an Application Online Start Here Programs Online Admissions Cost & Aid Online Student Support Online Student Life Explore Online Programs Start an Application Who We Are Meet Our Students Meet the Classes Meet Our Faculty About Asbury Leadership Theological Heritage & Distinctives News and Media Events Accreditation Athletics Alumni Alumni Home Reunion Alumni Board Ambassador Magazine Resources Chapel Campus Safety Faculty & Staff Directory Offices Registrar Provost Student Accounts Kinlaw Library Information for... Alumni Giving to Asbury More About Asbury About Asbury Life The College Tour Academy Dual Enrollment Title IX Conferences and Camps News & Media Calendar My Asbury Faculty & Staff Directory Secret Link We use cookies to ensure that we give you the best experience on our website. If you continue to use this site we will assume that you are happy with it. Accept"
    },
    "https://www.asbury.edu/about/offices/human-resources/jobs/postings/181638/": {
      "title": "Registrar",
      "description": "Registrar | www.asbury.edu Skip to content Undergraduate Start Here Programs Admissions Cost & Financial Aid Life at Asbury Student Support Athletics Find Your Major Virtual Tour Visit Apply Graduate Start Here Programs Graduate Student Admissions Cost & Aid Graduate Student Support Graduate Student Life Explore Degree Programs Schedule a Visit Start an Application Online Start Here Programs Online Admissions Cost & Aid Online Student Support Online Student Life Explore Online Programs Start an Application Who We Are Meet Our Students Meet the Classes Meet Our Faculty About Asbury Leadership Theological Heritage & Distinctives News and Media Events Accreditation Toggle search interface Toggle extended navigation Apply Visit Request info Give home About Registrar Registrar Job Details Department: Administrators Job Type: Staff Status: Exempt Deadline: Until Filled Reports to : Provost Job Purpose: The Registrar reports to the Provost, directs processes to ensure the integrity of the academic credits given and degrees earned by providing administrative supervision of the registrar’s office and overseeing all recordkeeping in support of the academic curriculum.  An important part of the position is supporting the ministry and mission of the University and advancing the academic excellence and spiritual vitality of our University and students. Each employee plays an important role in the development of the Christian faith in our students. Apply at jobs.asbury.edu Essential Functions: Ensure the academic integrity of academic credits given and degrees earned by providing administrative oversight and monitoring of the academic experience offered to students. Supervise and develop the staff of the Registrar’s office. Recruit and retain a high quality staff in the Registrar’s office. Provide training and development opportunities to enable staff to grow in their capacities and skills. Evaluate and submit annual performance reviews of Registrar’s office staff. Promote a collaborative workplace. Create and maintain avenues for evaluation of processes and policies. Direct the activities of the registrar’s office: Administer registration, transcript production, and grading processes Administer the budgets of the registrar’s office Supervise the ordering of supplies Provide leadership in planning Administer and coordinate the assignment of all classrooms Direct the verification of enrollment and degree progress for current and non-current students Certify credentials as needed Supervise student employees Validate faculty load issues as needed Coordinate details with the student accounts and financial aid offices Input all courses fees. Advise the Provost on all matters relating to the integrity of the curriculum and as a resource to committees as needed Provide leadership in issues related to the implementation of technology as it relates to academic records. Facilitate communication between offices that gather campus data and provide information related to registration enrollment to the Provost and other individuals on campus. Maintain enrollment and curricular histories for the university. Prepare reports as needed for decision making by the Provost and other campus officials. Interpret federal and state laws and regulations regarding FERPA, statistical reporting, academic transcript administration, and academic transcript administration. Represent the university externally in those networks dealing with academic record keeping and certification of student achievement. Serve on the academic committees as assigned. Work to identify at risk students and coordinate retention services with other departments. Work with the Provost to facilitate course evaluations for each faculty. Supervise the evaluation of transcripts for all students. Other duties as assigned. Physical requirements: While performing the duties of this job, the employee is regularly required to talk or hear. The employee frequently is required to stand; walk; use hands to finger, handle or feel; and reach with hands and arms.  This position requires the ability to occasionally lift items, up to 25 pounds. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work: This is a full-time position, and normal work hours are Monday through Friday, 8:00 a.m. to 5 This position requires additional hours and weekend Travel: Minimal travel is expected for this position. Qualifications: Master’s degree from an accredited college or Minimum of 5 years’ experience required as registrar, assistant registrar, or other administrative/faculty member at a higher education institution with significant administration experience with academic records. Demonstrated skills and administration organization, problem solving, and personnel management. Demonstrated commitment to staff development. Innovative and energetic leadership style Understanding of policy in general and its role and implementation in an organization Ability to work effectively as a colleague with university administrators, faculty, staff, and students. Experience with computerized integrated student records systems Strong interpersonal and communication A committed and dynamic Christian faith is vital along with the ability to support the University’s theological position, lifestyle standards and Other Duties: Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities may change at any time with or without notice. Institutional Commitment: Asbury University is an independent, Christian, liberal arts university in the Wesleyan-Holiness tradition. In the desire to be a more inclusive community, reflective of the Kingdom of God, we especially encourage applications from women and from candidates from various ethnic backgrounds. At Asbury University, employees must display a committed and dynamic Christian faith along with the ability to support the University’s theological position, lifestyle standards, and mission. Candidates must agree, support and adhere to University policies and procedures – including the Faculty Manual, Community Standards Guidelines, Human Sexuality Statement, and the Standard of Conduct for employees. Asbury University does not discriminate on the basis of race, national origin, gender, or handicap in its educational programs, activities, or employment practices. One Macklem Drive • Wilmore, KY 40390 (859) 858-3511 Facebook Instagram Linkedin Youtube Mic Accreditation Calendar Campus Safety Chapel Directory Faculty Resources Jobs at Asbury Kinlaw Library My Asbury Site Accessibility Student Accounts This is Asbury Podcast Title IX © Copyright 2026 Asbury University Legal Notices Privacy Policy Title IX Non-Discrimination Student Code of Conduct Report an Issue with this Page Close navigation Apply Visit Request info Give Search Site Search Undergraduate Start Here Programs Admissions Cost & Financial Aid Life at Asbury Student Support Athletics Find Your Major Virtual Tour Visit Apply Graduate Start Here Programs Graduate Student Admissions Cost & Aid Graduate Student Support Graduate Student Life Explore Degree Programs Schedule a Visit Start an Application Online Start Here Programs Online Admissions Cost & Aid Online Student Support Online Student Life Explore Online Programs Start an Application Who We Are Meet Our Students Meet the Classes Meet Our Faculty About Asbury Leadership Theological Heritage & Distinctives News and Media Events Accreditation Athletics Alumni Alumni Home Reunion Alumni Board Ambassador Magazine Resources Chapel Campus Safety Faculty & Staff Directory Offices Registrar Provost Student Accounts Kinlaw Library Information for... Alumni Giving to Asbury More About Asbury About Asbury Life The College Tour Academy Dual Enrollment Title IX Conferences and Camps News & Media Calendar My Asbury Faculty & Staff Directory Secret Link We use cookies to ensure that we give you the best experience on our website. If you continue to use this site we will assume that you are happy with it. Accept"
    },
    "https://www.asbury.edu/about/offices/human-resources/jobs/postings/182641/": {
      "title": "Cheerleading - Head Coach (part time position)",
      "description": "Cheerleading - Head Coach (part time position) | www.asbury.edu Skip to content Undergraduate Start Here Programs Admissions Cost & Financial Aid Life at Asbury Student Support Athletics Find Your Major Virtual Tour Visit Apply Graduate Start Here Programs Graduate Student Admissions Cost & Aid Graduate Student Support Graduate Student Life Explore Degree Programs Schedule a Visit Start an Application Online Start Here Programs Online Admissions Cost & Aid Online Student Support Online Student Life Explore Online Programs Start an Application Who We Are Meet Our Students Meet the Classes Meet Our Faculty About Asbury Leadership Theological Heritage & Distinctives News and Media Events Accreditation Toggle search interface Toggle extended navigation Apply Visit Request info Give home About Cheerleading – Head Coach (part time position) Cheerleading – Head Coach (part time position) Job Details Department: Coaching Job Type: Staff Status: Exempt Deadline: Until Filled Apply by sending a resume, cover letter, and complete an application at https://jobs.asbury.edu/ Job Purpose: Coaches at Asbury University (AU) are expected to not simply coach teams, but rather build programs. The guiding philosophy for coaches is to “Recruit, Disciple and Build.” Essential responsibilities are focused on the following areas: Discipleship, Recruiting, Pursuing Excellence, Servant Leadership and Administration. Essential Functions: Instructing student athletes in cheerleading including teaching theory, techniques, and strategies of the team. Instructing student athletes in preparing their minds and bodies for optimum performance of the team including personal nutrition, physical fitness and overall physical, mental and spiritual health. Selection of team through a tryout process.  (This will include both men and women and the number of team members may vary from year to year, depending on the talent). Ensure that all Cheerleading team members understand the commitment that a team member must make if selected to be a member of the Asbury University team. Monitor the academic success of all team members. Exercise reasonable judgment in the stunts that team members are expected to perform. Enforce team member use of all appropriate safety equipment such as spotting belts, spotting harnesses, crash pads, etc., when learning new stunts and ensure continued use until both the student and coach feels confident that the student can perform the stunt. General administrative duties related to team functioning including: Ensuring all equipment is properly stored, and the building is secure after all practices. Picking up and returning vans before and after performances. Loading and unloading team equipment for performances. Ensure student drivers have filled out the necessary paperwork to be approved as drivers (juniors and seniors only). Ensure availability of a first aid kit at each practice and performance and that check to see that it has the necessary supplies. Inspect all equipment to ensure each piece is in safe, usable condition. Other duties as assigned Physical Requirements: While performing the duties of this job, the employee is regularly required to talk or hear. The employee frequently is required to stand; walk; use hands to finger, handle or feel; and reach with hands and arms.  Majority of the work performed will be at the sports venue. Some work will be performed in an office environment. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work : This is a part-time, stipend position, and hours of work and days vary according to practice and game schedule.  Depending on the season, work includes evenings and weekends. Travel: Some travel is expected for this position. Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree preferred. 3-5 years minimum related coaching experience. A committed and dynamic Christian faith is vital along with the ability to support the University’s theological position, lifestyle standards and mission. Other Duties: Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties, or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. One Macklem Drive • Wilmore, KY 40390 (859) 858-3511 Facebook Instagram Linkedin Youtube Mic Accreditation Calendar Campus Safety Chapel Directory Faculty Resources Jobs at Asbury Kinlaw Library My Asbury Site Accessibility Student Accounts This is Asbury Podcast Title IX © Copyright 2026 Asbury University Legal Notices Privacy Policy Title IX Non-Discrimination Student Code of Conduct Report an Issue with this Page Close navigation Apply Visit Request info Give Search Site Search Undergraduate Start Here Programs Admissions Cost & Financial Aid Life at Asbury Student Support Athletics Find Your Major Virtual Tour Visit Apply Graduate Start Here Programs Graduate Student Admissions Cost & Aid Graduate Student Support Graduate Student Life Explore Degree Programs Schedule a Visit Start an Application Online Start Here Programs Online Admissions Cost & Aid Online Student Support Online Student Life Explore Online Programs Start an Application Who We Are Meet Our Students Meet the Classes Meet Our Faculty About Asbury Leadership Theological Heritage & Distinctives News and Media Events Accreditation Athletics Alumni Alumni Home Reunion Alumni Board Ambassador Magazine Resources Chapel Campus Safety Faculty & Staff Directory Offices Registrar Provost Student Accounts Kinlaw Library Information for... Alumni Giving to Asbury More About Asbury About Asbury Life The College Tour Academy Dual Enrollment Title IX Conferences and Camps News & Media Calendar My Asbury Faculty & Staff Directory Secret Link We use cookies to ensure that we give you the best experience on our website. If you continue to use this site we will assume that you are happy with it. Accept"
    },
    "https://www.asbury.edu/about/offices/human-resources/jobs/postings/182683/": {
      "title": "Soccer (Men's) - Head Coach",
      "description": "Soccer (Men's) - Head Coach | www.asbury.edu Skip to content Undergraduate Start Here Programs Admissions Cost & Financial Aid Life at Asbury Student Support Athletics Find Your Major Virtual Tour Visit Apply Graduate Start Here Programs Graduate Student Admissions Cost & Aid Graduate Student Support Graduate Student Life Explore Degree Programs Schedule a Visit Start an Application Online Start Here Programs Online Admissions Cost & Aid Online Student Support Online Student Life Explore Online Programs Start an Application Who We Are Meet Our Students Meet the Classes Meet Our Faculty About Asbury Leadership Theological Heritage & Distinctives News and Media Events Accreditation Toggle search interface Toggle extended navigation Apply Visit Request info Give home About Soccer (Men’s) – Head Coach Soccer (Men’s) – Head Coach Job Details Department: Coaching Job Type: Staff Status: Exempt Deadline: Until Filled Apply by sending a resume, cover letter, and complete an application at https://jobs.asbury.edu/ Position to be filled January 2027. Duties and Responsibilities: Coaches at Asbury University (AU) are expected to not simply coach teams, but rather build programs. The guiding philosophy for coaches is to “Recruit, Disciple and Build.” Essential responsibilities are focused on the following areas: Discipleship, Recruiting, Pursuing Excellence, Servant Leadership and Administration. Primary Duties : Responsible for management and development of all aspects of a collegiate men’s soccer program but not limited to: Discipleship of the students in the program Teaching and modeling the value of Christian competition Recruiting and retaining quality student-athletes who value and understand Asbury’s mission and vision Overseeing all aspects of the intercollegiate team with a target roster of 32 players Hiring and supervising assistant coaches and team managers Planning, oversight and administration of the soccer budget Organizing, planning and scheduling all practices and competitions Monitoring academic performance of student-athletes and partnering with Student Development for discipleship, development and retention of student-athletes Conducting summer and identification soccer camps Coordinating team travel (transportation, lodging, meals, itineraries, class excuses) Creating service and mission opportunities for student-athletes to positively impact the community Coordinating and leading annual crowd-funding initiative (eTeamSponsor) for men’s soccer program Continuing the men’s soccer alumni communication plan with the goal of hosting an annual on-campus alumni event. Other Duties: Assist the Athletic Department staff with operational roles including: event management, marketing, student-athlete services, and facilities. Assist with annual Athletic Department events including: Eagle Awards and Golf Fundraiser. Other duties as assigned. Job Skills and Specifications Exhibit and articulate evidence of current, practical knowledge of the sport of men’s soccer. Exhibit and articulate evidence of a personal relationship with Jesus Christ. Ability to become knowledgeable of, support and uphold the philosophy of both Asbury University and the Asbury Athletic Department. Exhibit professionalism at all times. This applies to conduct, appearance, and fulfillment of job responsibilities.  Be an example in word and action. Demonstrate concern with the total development and welfare of each student-athlete not just athletic development, but spiritual, educational, moral and social development as well. Continually strive for personal growth physically, spiritually, mentally and  socially. Qualifications : Bachelor’s Degree from an accredited 4-year institution, Master’s preferred. Experience in coaching soccer at the collegiate level coaching preferred. Commitment to provide positive experiences for student athletes in the soccer program. Exhibit a commitment to abide by all University, conference, NCAA Division III, NCCAA rules and guidelines. Experience with and commitment to working with diverse student populations. A committed and dynamic Christian faith is vital along with the ability to support the University’s theological position, lifestyle standards and mission. One Macklem Drive • Wilmore, KY 40390 (859) 858-3511 Facebook Instagram Linkedin Youtube Mic Accreditation Calendar Campus Safety Chapel Directory Faculty Resources Jobs at Asbury Kinlaw Library My Asbury Site Accessibility Student Accounts This is Asbury Podcast Title IX © Copyright 2026 Asbury University Legal Notices Privacy Policy Title IX Non-Discrimination Student Code of Conduct Report an Issue with this Page Close navigation Apply Visit Request info Give Search Site Search Undergraduate Start Here Programs Admissions Cost & Financial Aid Life at Asbury Student Support Athletics Find Your Major Virtual Tour Visit Apply Graduate Start Here Programs Graduate Student Admissions Cost & Aid Graduate Student Support Graduate Student Life Explore Degree Programs Schedule a Visit Start an Application Online Start Here Programs Online Admissions Cost & Aid Online Student Support Online Student Life Explore Online Programs Start an Application Who We Are Meet Our Students Meet the Classes Meet Our Faculty About Asbury Leadership Theological Heritage & Distinctives News and Media Events Accreditation Athletics Alumni Alumni Home Reunion Alumni Board Ambassador Magazine Resources Chapel Campus Safety Faculty & Staff Directory Offices Registrar Provost Student Accounts Kinlaw Library Information for... Alumni Giving to Asbury More About Asbury About Asbury Life The College Tour Academy Dual Enrollment Title IX Conferences and Camps News & Media Calendar My Asbury Faculty & Staff Directory Secret Link We use cookies to ensure that we give you the best experience on our website. If you continue to use this site we will assume that you are happy with it. Accept"
    },
    "https://www.asbury.edu/about/offices/human-resources/jobs/postings/183080/": {
      "title": "Equine Center Weekend Caretaker",
      "description": "Equine Center Weekend Caretaker | www.asbury.edu Skip to content Undergraduate Start Here Programs Admissions Cost & Financial Aid Life at Asbury Student Support Athletics Find Your Major Virtual Tour Visit Apply Graduate Start Here Programs Graduate Student Admissions Cost & Aid Graduate Student Support Graduate Student Life Explore Degree Programs Schedule a Visit Start an Application Online Start Here Programs Online Admissions Cost & Aid Online Student Support Online Student Life Explore Online Programs Start an Application Who We Are Meet Our Students Meet the Classes Meet Our Faculty About Asbury Leadership Theological Heritage & Distinctives News and Media Events Accreditation Toggle search interface Toggle extended navigation Apply Visit Request info Give home About Equine Center Weekend Caretaker Equine Center Weekend Caretaker Job Details Department: Other Job Type: Staff Status: Non-Exempt Deadline: Until Filled Apply at jobs.asbury.edu Reports to: Equine Center Director Job Purpose: The Equine Center Weekend Caretaker is responsible for the daily care, feeding, and well-being of horses as well as the upkeep of the Equine Center on Saturday and Sunday. Essential Functions: Feed and water horses according to individualized feeding schedules. Turn out and bring in horses safely between stalls and paddocks. Clean stalls, paddocks, and barn aisles; dispose of manure and bedding appropriately. Monitor horses for signs of illness, injury, or distress; promptly report any concerns to the Equine Center Director. Maintain cleanliness of tack rooms, restrooms, and common areas. Refill hay, bedding, and feed supplies as needed. Assist with basic facility maintenance (e.g., fence checks, water trough cleaning). Ensure all barn doors, gates, and equipment are properly secured at the end of each shift. Provide excellent animal welfare and uphold the Equine Center’s safety and cleanliness standards. Maintain familiarity with local veterinarian and communicate effectively with the Equine Center staff regarding when to call the veterinarian; assist by safely holding horses for veterinary visits; relay all veterinary treatment and doctoring instructions clearly and accurately to Equine Center staff. Qualifications: Prior experience handling and caring for horses is required. Strong understanding of horse behavior, safety, and daily care routines. Ability to work independently and manage time effectively. Reliable, punctual, and attentive to detail. Physically capable of lifting up to 50 pounds and performing manual labor in varying weather conditions. Must have reliable transportation. Institutional Commitment: Asbury University is an independent, Christian, liberal arts university in the Wesleyan-Holiness tradition. In the desire to be a more inclusive community, reflective of the Kingdom of God, we especially encourage applications from women and from candidates from various ethnic backgrounds. At Asbury University, employees must display a committed and dynamic Christian faith along with the ability to support the University’s theological position, lifestyle standards, and mission. Candidates must agree, support and adhere to University policies and procedures – including the Faculty Manual, Community Standards Guidelines, Human Sexuality Statement, and the Standard of Conduct for employees. Asbury University does not discriminate on the basis of race, national origin, gender, or handicap in its educational programs, activities, or employment practices. One Macklem Drive • Wilmore, KY 40390 (859) 858-3511 Facebook Instagram Linkedin Youtube Mic Accreditation Calendar Campus Safety Chapel Directory Faculty Resources Jobs at Asbury Kinlaw Library My Asbury Site Accessibility Student Accounts This is Asbury Podcast Title IX © Copyright 2026 Asbury University Legal Notices Privacy Policy Title IX Non-Discrimination Student Code of Conduct Report an Issue with this Page Close navigation Apply Visit Request info Give Search Site Search Undergraduate Start Here Programs Admissions Cost & Financial Aid Life at Asbury Student Support Athletics Find Your Major Virtual Tour Visit Apply Graduate Start Here Programs Graduate Student Admissions Cost & Aid Graduate Student Support Graduate Student Life Explore Degree Programs Schedule a Visit Start an Application Online Start Here Programs Online Admissions Cost & Aid Online Student Support Online Student Life Explore Online Programs Start an Application Who We Are Meet Our Students Meet the Classes Meet Our Faculty About Asbury Leadership Theological Heritage & Distinctives News and Media Events Accreditation Athletics Alumni Alumni Home Reunion Alumni Board Ambassador Magazine Resources Chapel Campus Safety Faculty & Staff Directory Offices Registrar Provost Student Accounts Kinlaw Library Information for... Alumni Giving to Asbury More About Asbury About Asbury Life The College Tour Academy Dual Enrollment Title IX Conferences and Camps News & Media Calendar My Asbury Faculty & Staff Directory Secret Link We use cookies to ensure that we give you the best experience on our website. If you continue to use this site we will assume that you are happy with it. Accept"
