    "https://www.asbury.edu/about/offices/human-resources/jobs/postings/96959/": {
      "title": "Security Officer Fill-In",
      "description": "Security Officer Fill-In | www.asbury.edu Skip to content Undergraduate Start Here Programs Admissions Cost & Financial Aid Life at Asbury Student Support Athletics Find Your Major Virtual Tour Visit Apply Graduate Start Here Programs Graduate Student Admissions Cost & Aid Graduate Student Support Graduate Student Life Explore Degree Programs Schedule a Visit Start an Application Online Start Here Programs Online Admissions Cost & Aid Online Student Support Online Student Life Explore Online Programs Start an Application Who We Are Meet Our Students Meet the Classes Meet Our Faculty About Asbury Leadership Theological Heritage & Distinctives News and Media Events Accreditation Toggle search interface Toggle extended navigation Apply Visit Request info Give home About Security Officer Fill-In Security Officer Fill-In Job Details Department: Other Job Type: Staff Status: Non-Exempt Deadline: Until Filled Asbury University is looking for a qualified candidate to fill our open Security Officer Fill-In role. Job Purpose : As a uniformed officer of the peace, under the direction of the manager, works to promote a safe and secure campus environment for students, employees and guests. Essential Functions: Duties: Provides security services. Patrols University buildings & property. Patrols assigned areas and checks for fire and safety hazards, intruders or any suspicious circumstances. Aids University officials in crowd & traffic control, disturbance of the peace, mischief and/or misconduct of students or visitors Assists in locking/unlocking of buildings, directs visitors for parking. Accept other duties as assigned Critical Physical Demands: Occasionally able to sit and squat Occasionally able to lift, work overhead, and perform fine manipulation Frequently able to stand and bend Frequently able to grasp, push and pull Frequently able to climb stairs and ladders Frequently able to walk into any area of campus. Respond to campus fire alarms and campus accidents Must be able to consistently work 3rd shift Works independently Skill Requirements: Must be able to read and write Experience and Training: 1-2 years experience as a security officer, police officer or equivalent preferred. Temporary or fill-in security officer may require less experience. Education: High School diploma or equivalent preferred. Supervision Received: Receives full instructions initially from the Security & environmental Safety Manager. On job training with training officer before working independently. Daily shift instructions provided as need. Other requirements : Must successfully complete a pre-employment drug screen and background check . A committed and dynamic Christian faith is vital along with the ability to support the University’s theological position, lifestyle standards and mission. Institutional Commitment: Asbury University is an independent, Christian, liberal arts university in the Wesleyan-Holiness tradition. In the desire to be a more inclusive community, reflective of the Kingdom of God, we especially encourage applications from women and from candidates from various ethnic backgrounds. At Asbury University, employees must display a committed and dynamic Christian faith along with the ability to support the University’s theological position, lifestyle standards, and mission. Candidates must agree, support and adhere to University policies and procedures – including the Faculty Manual, Community Standards Guidelines, Human Sexuality Statement, and the Standard of Conduct for employees. Asbury University does not discriminate on the basis of race, national origin, gender, or handicap in its educational programs, activities, or employment practices. Application Process: Interested parties may forward their completed Asbury University Application , signed Application Insert and required essay (located at the bottom of the application insert), and resume to the Human Resources Office via email at human.resources@asbury.edu or by mail at: Human Resources Asbury University 1 Macklem Drive Wilmore, KY 40390 One Macklem Drive • Wilmore, KY 40390 (859) 858-3511 Facebook Instagram Linkedin Youtube Mic Accreditation Calendar Campus Safety Chapel Directory Faculty Resources Jobs at Asbury Kinlaw Library My Asbury Site Accessibility Student Accounts This is Asbury Podcast Title IX © Copyright 2026 Asbury University Legal Notices Privacy Policy Title IX Non-Discrimination Student Code of Conduct Report an Issue with this Page Close navigation Apply Visit Request info Give Search Site Search Undergraduate Start Here Programs Admissions Cost & Financial Aid Life at Asbury Student Support Athletics Find Your Major Virtual Tour Visit Apply Graduate Start Here Programs Graduate Student Admissions Cost & Aid Graduate Student Support Graduate Student Life Explore Degree Programs Schedule a Visit Start an Application Online Start Here Programs Online Admissions Cost & Aid Online Student Support Online Student Life Explore Online Programs Start an Application Who We Are Meet Our Students Meet the Classes Meet Our Faculty About Asbury Leadership Theological Heritage & Distinctives News and Media Events Accreditation Athletics Alumni Alumni Home Reunion Alumni Board Ambassador Magazine Resources Chapel Campus Safety Faculty & Staff Directory Offices Registrar Provost Student Accounts Kinlaw Library Information for... Alumni Giving to Asbury More About Asbury About Asbury Life The College Tour Academy Dual Enrollment Title IX Conferences and Camps News & Media Calendar My Asbury Faculty & Staff Directory Secret Link We use cookies to ensure that we give you the best experience on our website. If you continue to use this site we will assume that you are happy with it. Accept"
