    "https://www.asbury.edu/about/offices/human-resources/jobs/postings/181033/": {
      "title": "Benefits and Payroll Manager",
      "description": "Benefits and Payroll Manager | www.asbury.edu Skip to content Undergraduate Start Here Programs Admissions Cost & Financial Aid Life at Asbury Student Support Athletics Find Your Major Virtual Tour Visit Apply Graduate Start Here Programs Graduate Student Admissions Cost & Aid Graduate Student Support Graduate Student Life Explore Degree Programs Schedule a Visit Start an Application Online Start Here Programs Online Admissions Cost & Aid Online Student Support Online Student Life Explore Online Programs Start an Application Who We Are Meet Our Students Meet the Classes Meet Our Faculty About Asbury Leadership Theological Heritage & Distinctives News and Media Events Accreditation Toggle search interface Toggle extended navigation Apply Visit Request info Give home About Benefits and Payroll Manager Benefits and Payroll Manager Job Details Department: Professional/Administrative Staff Job Type: Staff Status: Exempt Deadline: Until Filled Reports to : Assoc. VP of Human Resources, Risk Management, and Project Manager Job Purpose : The Benefits and Payroll Manager is a key member of the Human Resources team and assists in all areas of Human Resources.  The position has primary responsibility for the daily administration of all employee benefits plans and payroll. Meets with employees to discuss and resolve any benefit questions or issues that arise. Oversees the distribution of all relevant compensation materials and ensures that all requests for payment are made in a timely manner and fall within budgetary limits. An important part of the position is supporting the ministry and mission of the University and advancing the academic excellence and spiritual vitality of our University and students. Each employee plays an important role in the development of the Christian faith in our students. Essential Functions: Benefits Administration Administration of all employee benefits plans including meeting with every new benefit eligible employee. Coordinates on boarding of all benefit eligible employees. Develops communication pieces (including print, electronic, and web) for annual open enrollment and ongoing benefit information. Maintains all benefit enrollment and termination records and ensures compliance with all applicable benefit regulations and laws. Coordinates annual benefit open enrollment. Manages the resolution of claims and billing issues. Reviews and recommends implementation of renewal and new benefit contracts. Oversees the tuition waiver program and graduate loan program and tracks data on program usage. Oversees the enrollment and education processes of the retirement plan. Coordinates all appropriate exit materials, performs exit interviews for all exiting employees, and tracks responses to exit survey materials. Manages and coordinates annual retirement plan audit. Payroll Administration Works directly with Assoc VP regarding all aspects of university payroll, including time and attendance, payroll processing, tax withholding and submittal, and implementation of University payroll policy. Updates the Payroll system for regular employee data and works to maintains accurate records of employee compensation and other matters. Compensation Works with various campus offices and departments to ensure timely and accurate processing of payment requests. Workers Compensation Works directly with the insurance carrier and employee for all workers compensation claims. Maintains OSHA 300 log and files annual report. General HR duties Maintains all employee files both paper and electronic, assists with the development and updating of policies for the Employee Handbook. Works with the AVP to oversee the performance management process including preparation and distribution of evaluations, receiving completed forms, scoring, and statistical tracking of performance data. Works directly with the AVP for the management of all special events overseen by the HR Office. This includes employee Christmas celebration, new employee orientation, retirement/farewell receptions and other trainings/programs. Issues all FML notices and tracks FML time for applicable employees as well as meets with employees and supervisors to educate them on FML. Supervises student workers in the office. May assist the AVP in conducting employee relations meetings. Oversees the employee recognition program including tracking years of service as well as ordering awards and preparation of certificates. In the absence of the AVP may assist in supervision of the HR Assistant. Regularly updates the AVP of Human Resources and Risk Management on all matters related to the operations of the HR office. Assists the AVP with legal matters or other projects, as determined by the AVP. Other duties as assigned. Physical Requirements: While performing the duties of this job, the employee is regularly required to talk or hear. The employee frequently is required to stand; walk; use hands to finger, handle or feel; and reach with hands and arms.  This position requires the ability to occasionally lift office products and supplies, up to 20 pounds. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work : This is a full-time on-site position, and hours of work and days are Monday through Friday, 8:00 a.m. to 5 p.m. Travel: No travel is expected for this position. Qualifications : A bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university (candidates with over ten years of benefits or human resources experience may substitute experience for a degree). 3-5 years of previous benefits administration and/or human resources experience. A high degree of proficiency with word processing and spreadsheet functions. Excellent customer service skills. An ability to appropriately work with highly confidential material. Excellent technological, verbal and written communication skills. Human resources certification is preferred (PHR, SHRM-CP). A committed and dynamic Christian faith is vital along with the ability to support the University’s theological position, lifestyle standards and mission. Other Duties : Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities may change at any time with or without notice. Institutional Commitment: Asbury University is an independent, Christian, liberal arts university in the Wesleyan-Holiness tradition. In the desire to be a more inclusive community, reflective of the Kingdom of God, we especially encourage applications from women and from candidates from various ethnic backgrounds. At Asbury University, employees must display a committed and dynamic Christian faith along with the ability to support the University’s theological position, lifestyle standards, and mission. Candidates must agree, support and adhere to University policies and procedures – including the Faculty Manual, Community Standards Guidelines, Human Sexuality Statement, and the Standard of Conduct for employees. Asbury University does not discriminate on the basis of race, national origin, gender, or handicap in its educational programs, activities, or employment practices. Apply by send resume, cover letter, and application through the employment portal at employment applications . One Macklem Drive • Wilmore, KY 40390 (859) 858-3511 Facebook Instagram Linkedin Youtube Mic Accreditation Calendar Campus Safety Chapel Directory Faculty Resources Jobs at Asbury Kinlaw Library My Asbury Site Accessibility Student Accounts This is Asbury Podcast Title IX © Copyright 2026 Asbury University Legal Notices Privacy Policy Title IX Non-Discrimination Student Code of Conduct Report an Issue with this Page Close navigation Apply Visit Request info Give Search Site Search Undergraduate Start Here Programs Admissions Cost & Financial Aid Life at Asbury Student Support Athletics Find Your Major Virtual Tour Visit Apply Graduate Start Here Programs Graduate Student Admissions Cost & Aid Graduate Student Support Graduate Student Life Explore Degree Programs Schedule a Visit Start an Application Online Start Here Programs Online Admissions Cost & Aid Online Student Support Online Student Life Explore Online Programs Start an Application Who We Are Meet Our Students Meet the Classes Meet Our Faculty About Asbury Leadership Theological Heritage & Distinctives News and Media Events Accreditation Athletics Alumni Alumni Home Reunion Alumni Board Ambassador Magazine Resources Chapel Campus Safety Faculty & Staff Directory Offices Registrar Provost Student Accounts Kinlaw Library Information for... Alumni Giving to Asbury More About Asbury About Asbury Life The College Tour Academy Dual Enrollment Title IX Conferences and Camps News & Media Calendar My Asbury Faculty & Staff Directory Secret Link We use cookies to ensure that we give you the best experience on our website. If you continue to use this site we will assume that you are happy with it. Accept"
    },
    "https://www.asbury.edu/about/offices/human-resources/jobs/postings/180061/": {
      "title": "Counselor",
      "description": "Counselor | www.asbury.edu Skip to content Undergraduate Start Here Programs Admissions Cost & Financial Aid Life at Asbury Student Support Athletics Find Your Major Virtual Tour Visit Apply Graduate Start Here Programs Graduate Student Admissions Cost & Aid Graduate Student Support Graduate Student Life Explore Degree Programs Schedule a Visit Start an Application Online Start Here Programs Online Admissions Cost & Aid Online Student Support Online Student Life Explore Online Programs Start an Application Who We Are Meet Our Students Meet the Classes Meet Our Faculty About Asbury Leadership Theological Heritage & Distinctives News and Media Events Accreditation Toggle search interface Toggle extended navigation Apply Visit Request info Give home About Counselor Counselor Job Details Department: Professional/Administrative Staff Job Type: Staff Status: Exempt Deadline: Until Filled Apply at jobs.asbury.edu Job Purpose: The Counselor provides programs and services to address the mental health needs of the entire campus community. This counselor will provide a full range of community counseling services and is responsible for specific components of the departmental goal plan. The Counselor serves directly under the Associate Dean of Wholeness and Wellness. As a staff member of the Center for Wholeness and Wellness and the Student Life team, the counselor supports the overall mission of Asbury University and adheres to the ethos statement of the University. An important part of the position is supporting the ministry and mission of the University and advancing the academic excellence and spiritual vitality of our University and students. Each employee plays an important role in the development of the Christian faith in our students. Essential Functions: Primary focus of this position is to provide individual, couple, and group counseling services and referral services as part of the Center for Wholeness and Wellness in accord with established policies and procedures. Caseload would be approximately 20-25 hours per week with individual, couples and group counseling. To provide assessment services to students. To participate in multidisciplinary case consultations as permitted by professional ethics and legal statute. To provide multidisciplinary training opportunities that include practicum/intern orientation, Friday training component of the practicum/internship program, suicide prevention programs as well as Student Life and other staff/faculty development programs. To provide consultations with administration, faculty, and/or staff regarding students as permitted by professional ethics and legal statute. To plan, implement, and evaluate campus programming provided by the Center for Wholeness and Wellness. To provide assistance in student-related mental health emergencies. Counselors are to be available after regular working hours on a rotating basis to provide crisis intervention for acute mental health emergencies. On-call scheduling is done at the beginning of each semester for professional staff. To provide consultation and assistance in Student Life programming. To provide weekly supervision and training for master’s level practicum/intern counselors. To accomplish tasks in accord with established professional ethical standards and best practice standards. Other tasks and duties as assigned. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work : This is a full-time, on-site position, 9 month position. The hours of work and days are Monday through Friday, 8:00 a.m. to 5 p.m. Potential exists to work some evenings and weekends. Travel: No travel is expected for this position. Qualifications: Master’s level or above counselor, psychologist or marriage and family therapist, licensed or eligible for licensure in Kentucky by hire date. Minimum of two (2) years’ experience and autonomous functioning. Required to maintain liability insurance coverage and current licensure throughout employment. Additional hours, evenings, and weekends occasionally required. A committed and dynamic Christian faith is vital along with the ability to support the University’s theological position, lifestyle standards and mission. Other Duties: Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. Institutional Commitment: Asbury University is an independent, Christian, liberal arts university in the Wesleyan-Holiness tradition. In the desire to be a more inclusive community, reflective of the Kingdom of God, we especially encourage applications from women and from candidates from various ethnic backgrounds. At Asbury University, employees must display a committed and dynamic Christian faith along with the ability to support the University’s theological position, lifestyle standards, and mission. Candidates must agree, support and adhere to University policies and procedures – including the Faculty Manual, Community Standards Guidelines, Human Sexuality Statement, and the Standard of Conduct for employees. Asbury University does not discriminate on the basis of race, national origin, gender, or handicap in its educational programs, activities, or employment practices. One Macklem Drive • Wilmore, KY 40390 (859) 858-3511 Facebook Instagram Linkedin Youtube Mic Accreditation Calendar Campus Safety Chapel Directory Faculty Resources Jobs at Asbury Kinlaw Library My Asbury Site Accessibility Student Accounts This is Asbury Podcast Title IX © Copyright 2026 Asbury University Legal Notices Privacy Policy Title IX Non-Discrimination Student Code of Conduct Report an Issue with this Page Close navigation Apply Visit Request info Give Search Site Search Undergraduate Start Here Programs Admissions Cost & Financial Aid Life at Asbury Student Support Athletics Find Your Major Virtual Tour Visit Apply Graduate Start Here Programs Graduate Student Admissions Cost & Aid Graduate Student Support Graduate Student Life Explore Degree Programs Schedule a Visit Start an Application Online Start Here Programs Online Admissions Cost & Aid Online Student Support Online Student Life Explore Online Programs Start an Application Who We Are Meet Our Students Meet the Classes Meet Our Faculty About Asbury Leadership Theological Heritage & Distinctives News and Media Events Accreditation Athletics Alumni Alumni Home Reunion Alumni Board Ambassador Magazine Resources Chapel Campus Safety Faculty & Staff Directory Offices Registrar Provost Student Accounts Kinlaw Library Information for... Alumni Giving to Asbury More About Asbury About Asbury Life The College Tour Academy Dual Enrollment Title IX Conferences and Camps News & Media Calendar My Asbury Faculty & Staff Directory Secret Link We use cookies to ensure that we give you the best experience on our website. If you continue to use this site we will assume that you are happy with it. Accept"
    },
    "https://www.asbury.edu/about/offices/human-resources/jobs/postings/182008/": {
      "title": "Executive Assistant - Provost and Senior VP of Academic Affairs",
      "description": "Executive Assistant - Provost and Senior VP of Academic Affairs | www.asbury.edu Skip to content Undergraduate Start Here Programs Admissions Cost & Financial Aid Life at Asbury Student Support Athletics Find Your Major Virtual Tour Visit Apply Graduate Start Here Programs Graduate Student Admissions Cost & Aid Graduate Student Support Graduate Student Life Explore Degree Programs Schedule a Visit Start an Application Online Start Here Programs Online Admissions Cost & Aid Online Student Support Online Student Life Explore Online Programs Start an Application Who We Are Meet Our Students Meet the Classes Meet Our Faculty About Asbury Leadership Theological Heritage & Distinctives News and Media Events Accreditation Toggle search interface Toggle extended navigation Apply Visit Request info Give home About Executive Assistant – Provost and Senior VP of Academic Affairs Executive Assistant – Provost and Senior VP of Academic Affairs Job Details Department: Professional/Administrative Staff Job Type: Staff Status: Exempt Deadline: Until Filled APPLICATION PROCESS: Interested candidates should complete an employment application at application and include a letter of interest and resume. Applications available at jobs.asbury.edu Job Purpose: The Executive Assistant to the Provost & Senior Vice President for Academic Affairs is a highly visible and impactful role responsible for assisting the Provost with daily operational and administrative details and performs competent, diverse, and complex administrative and office management functions that require recurring contact with senior leadership, board members, faculty, staff, students, alumni, donors, and external constituencies; a thorough knowledge of the University mission, policies, procedures, and operations; and an understanding of the University’s role within the community. As the Provost’s principal aide, the Executive Assistant serves as a liaison between the Provost’s Office, the faculty, staff, and those who engage with the office and demonstrates decorum, diplomacy, and tact along with excellent interpersonal, written and verbal communication skills. In managing the Provost’s fluid schedule along with events, meetings, activities, budgets, projects, correspondence, records, and front-desk reception, this professional exhibits confidentiality, initiative, independent judgment, and a commitment to excellence. An important part of the position is supporting the ministry and mission of the University and advancing the academic excellence and spiritual vitality of Asbury University and students. Each employee plays an important role in the development of the Christian faith in our students. Essential Functions: Facilitates efficient, effective, and strategic utilization of the Provost’s schedule through coordination of a complex and fluid calendar of events, meetings, operations, and tasks. Serves as gatekeeper and gateway. Plans weeks, months, and multiple academic years ahead when possible, tracking University and events involving the Provost. Schedules and organizes meetings and reservations by handling all preparation and follow-up pertaining to events and operations in Academic Affairs (e.g., catering, parking, and meeting confirmations). Provides appropriate materials and information to the Provost to ensure readiness for scheduled meetings, and daily operations in Academic Affairs. Provides support for the Provost when preparing materials for the Committee on Academic Affairs of the Board of Trustees. Maintains discretion and confidentiality with personnel files, correspondence, and information. Serves as an event coordinator and facilitates the success of special functions and events hosted by the Provost’s Office (e.g., annual faculty events, Asbury Colloquium, SEARCH, etc.). Arranges the Provost’s travel while coordinating with appropriate offices and/or organizations; prepares complex and detailed travel plans, itineraries, and agendas; informs Provost of important issues, activities, messages, and mail while away. Promotes a positive image of the University by greeting and receiving visitors to the Provost’s Office, responding to inquiries from diverse University publics (e.g., students, parents, faculty, staff, legislators, alumni, the media, and public and private officials), providing information regarding Asbury University policies or decisions, referring inquiries or problems to the appropriate office or person, and resolving problems. Evaluates and determines the most appropriate steps to assure the proper functioning and information flow of the Provost’s Office. Facilitates timely and appropriate communication between Deans, faculty, staff, students and external constituencies. Assists with answering mail received or other inquiries/situations; composes correspondence for Provost signature. Serves as the manager for the Provost’s Office and provides budget management for the daily operational work of the Office of the Provost & Senior Vice President for Academic Affairs and preparing faculty contracts, credit card reports, invoice payments, as well as maintaining office supplies. Monitor and track faculty development budget account lines and expenditures in collaboration with the Provost. May provide supervision to student workers or staff as assigned by the Provost. Responsible for maintaining all faculty personnel files, faculty roster accreditation materials, and faculty data in compliance with SACSCOC standards. Coordinates Commencement activities. Oversight of the Provost’s webpages. Accept other duties as assigned. Additional Responsibilities : Preparation of annual full and part-time faculty contracts (including salary calculation, actual contract preparation, and salary report preparation for Business Office/Payroll Office/Human Resources Office).  Maintain salary database system.  Prepare salary adjustments as needed. Assists the Provost in preparation of bi-annual board reports to the President and takes minutes at related board sub-committee (e.g., Committee on Academic Affairs). Assists in faculty promotion/tenure review by maintaining the logistics of the process and compiling files for review by Faculty Tenure & Promotion Committee, the Provost and the Board of Trustees. Makes arrangements for meetings of the Faculty Interview Committee. Responsible for logistical management of several programs/events (e.g., Faculty Retreat, Deans’ Council meetings, Faculty Appreciation Dinner, Baccalaureate/Commencement, Brown Bags, Faculty Development Committee Meetings, and Faculty Assembly). Brings to the attention of the Provost any activity, incident, or concern which has an impact on the operation of the institution and/or requires the decision of the cabinet or the President. Arrange the annual meeting of the Committee on Committees. Physical requirements: While performing the duties of this job, the employee is regularly required to talk or hear. The employee frequently is required to stand; walk; use hands to finger, handle or feel; and reach with hands and arms. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work : This is a full-time on-site position, and hours of work and days are Monday through Friday, 8:00 am to 5 p.m. Position may require employee to occasionally work some evenings for university events. Travel: Travel is not expected for this position. Qualifications : High School diploma required, Bachelor’s degree preferred; Minimum of 5-7 years office management experience; Ability to self-manage and function independently and proactively with little supervision, as well as ability to collaboratively work as part of a team; High level of confidentiality and integrity and able to demonstrate utmost discretion when handling sensitive matters and materials; Ability to exercise tact, judgment and diplomacy in a poised, professional manner while interacting with a variety of constituencies; Excellent interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills; Strong writing and proofreading skills; High attention to detail and follow-through; Good reasoning, analytical, and decision-making abilities; Expertise in Microsoft 365 (Outlook, Excel, Word, PowerPoint, Teams) and social media platforms; A committed and dynamic Christian faith is vital along with the ability to support the University’s theological position, lifestyle standards and mission. Other Duties : Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities may change at any time with or without notice. Institutional Commitment: Asbury University is an independent, Christian, liberal arts university in the Wesleyan-Holiness tradition. In the desire to be a more inclusive community, reflective of the Kingdom of God, we especially encourage applications from women and from candidates from various ethnic backgrounds. At Asbury University, employees must display a committed and dynamic Christian faith along with the ability to support the University’s theological position, lifestyle standards, and mission. Candidates must agree, support and adhere to University policies and procedures – including the Faculty Manual, Community Standards Guidelines, Human Sexuality Statement, and the Standard of Conduct for employees. Asbury University does not discriminate on the basis of race, national origin, gender, or handicap in its educational programs, activities, or employment practices. One Macklem Drive • Wilmore, KY 40390 (859) 858-3511 Facebook Instagram Linkedin Youtube Mic Accreditation Calendar Campus Safety Chapel Directory Faculty Resources Jobs at Asbury Kinlaw Library My Asbury Site Accessibility Student Accounts This is Asbury Podcast Title IX © Copyright 2026 Asbury University Legal Notices Privacy Policy Title IX Non-Discrimination Student Code of Conduct Report an Issue with this Page Close navigation Apply Visit Request info Give Search Site Search Undergraduate Start Here Programs Admissions Cost & Financial Aid Life at Asbury Student Support Athletics Find Your Major Virtual Tour Visit Apply Graduate Start Here Programs Graduate Student Admissions Cost & Aid Graduate Student Support Graduate Student Life Explore Degree Programs Schedule a Visit Start an Application Online Start Here Programs Online Admissions Cost & Aid Online Student Support Online Student Life Explore Online Programs Start an Application Who We Are Meet Our Students Meet the Classes Meet Our Faculty About Asbury Leadership Theological Heritage & Distinctives News and Media Events Accreditation Athletics Alumni Alumni Home Reunion Alumni Board Ambassador Magazine Resources Chapel Campus Safety Faculty & Staff Directory Offices Registrar Provost Student Accounts Kinlaw Library Information for... Alumni Giving to Asbury More About Asbury About Asbury Life The College Tour Academy Dual Enrollment Title IX Conferences and Camps News & Media Calendar My Asbury Faculty & Staff Directory Secret Link We use cookies to ensure that we give you the best experience on our website. If you continue to use this site we will assume that you are happy with it. Accept"
    }
